<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="mesh-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>About</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="page-hero__title" data-reveal>{{hero.title}}</h1>
    <p class="lede" data-reveal style="--i: 1">{{hero.lede}}</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="stat-strip on-dark" aria-label="At a glance">
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <div class="stat-strip__grid">
      {{#each stats}}
        <div class="stat" data-reveal style="--i: {{@index}}">
          <p class="stat__value">{{this.value}}</p>
          <p class="stat__label">{{this.label}}</p>
          <p class="stat__note">{{this.note}}</p>
        </div>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-light">
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <div class="rail">
      <div class="rail__aside" data-reveal>
        <span class="label label--onlight">The firm</span>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size: var(--step--1)">Brooklyn, New York. Founded {{company.founded}}.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal>
        <p class="t-sm">Providing IT Services is a technology services firm in New York. We build software, stand up data platforms, and run the operational teams that sit behind both — for companies across the United States and for international companies using New York as their first American office.</p>
        <p class="muted">The six practices exist under one roof deliberately. In a services market where most firms specialise in one thing and subcontract the rest, a problem that crosses a boundary — a reporting failure that is really a process failure, a support backlog that is really a product defect — turns into a procurement exercise rather than a fix. We would rather absorb that internally.</p>
        <p class="muted">Our view is that services relationships fail on communication far more often than on capability. The engineers are usually good enough. What goes wrong is that nobody says the schedule slipped until the deadline arrives, or the status report describes a different project from the one being built. Everything in the way we run engagements is an attempt to make that specific failure harder.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-dark">
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <div class="section__head mb-3" data-reveal>
      <span class="label">Commitments</span>
      <h2 class="t-xl">Four things we put in the contract</h2>
      <p class="lede">Not values. Terms — the kind you can hold us to when a project goes badly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="principles">
      {{#each principles}}
        <article class="principle" data-reveal style="--i: {{@index}}">
          <h3>{{this.title}}</h3>
          <p>{{this.body}}</p>
        </article>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-light">
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <div class="rail">
      <div class="rail__aside" data-reveal>
        <span class="label label--onlight">Engagement</span>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="section__head mb-3" data-reveal>
          <h2 class="t-xl">How a project runs, start to finish</h2>
        </div>
        <ol class="numbered">
          {{#each process}}
            <li>
              <div>
                <h3>{{this.name}} — <span class="muted" style="font-weight: 400">{{this.duration}}</span></h3>
                <p>{{this.body}}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          {{/each}}
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section on-dark">
  <div class="shell shell--wide">
    <div class="split">
      <div data-reveal>
        <span class="label">Where we are</span>
        <h2 class="t-lg mt-2 mb-2">New York, and the day it reaches</h2>
        <p class="muted mb-3" style="font-size: var(--step--1); line-height: 1.7">
          Eastern time is the one zone that reaches the whole American working day and
          still catches Europe: London is mid-afternoon when we open, San Francisco is
          mid-morning when most of our clients&rsquo; days end. One office, one schedule,
          and no handover note written for someone who will read it eight hours later.
        </p>
        <address class="footer__address" style="margin-top: 0">
          {{company.address.line1}}<br>
          {{company.address.line2}}<br>
          {{company.address.country}}<br>
          <a href="{{company.address.maps}}" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: var(--signal)">Open in Maps</a>
        </address>
      </div>

      <div data-reveal style="--i: 1">
        <span class="label">Local time in our hubs</span>
        <div class="hubs mt-2" data-hub-clocks>
          {{#each hubs}}
            <div class="hub" data-hub-zone="{{this.zone}}">
              <span class="hub__city">{{this.name}}</span>
              <span class="hub__time">--:--</span>
              <span class="hub__delta" data-hub-delta>{{this.offset}}h</span>
            </div>
          {{/each}}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{> cta}}
